Package: prescco
Type: Package
Title: Prediction Intervals Under a Right-Censored Covariate
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kihyun", "Han",
           email = "kqh5716@psu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Constructs prediction intervals for an outcome when a
  time-to-event covariate is subject to right-censoring. The package
  accommodates optional fully observed continuous and discrete covariates
  and provides maximum-likelihood estimation of working models for the
  censored covariate and censoring time, complete-case and SPARCC estimators
  of the outcome-model coefficients, and prediction intervals based on
  PRESCCO, split conformal prediction, full conformal prediction, and
  jackknife+. PRESCCO is doubly robust and semiparametrically efficient when
  both working nuisance models are correctly specified. The repository also
  includes a self-contained simulation study under 'sim/'. PRESCCO
  abbreviates PREdiction with Semiparametric efficiency under a
  right-Censored COvariate.
